Getting around can be one of the hardest parts of living with a disability or long-term condition. These schemes can save money and make journeys easier.

## In this guide

- [Blue Badge](/support/travel/blue-badge/): park closer to where you need to go
- [Disabled Persons Railcard](/support/travel/disabled-persons-railcard/): a third off most train fares, for you and a companion
- [Free bus passes](/support/travel/bus-passes/): free off-peak bus travel in England, and free travel at any time in Wales
- [Motability and car tax](/support/travel/motability-and-car-tax/): lease a car or scooter, and pay no or less car tax
- [Help when you travel](/support/travel/travel-assistance/): free assistance on trains, at airports and more

## Quick tips

- Many of these schemes accept a **PIP, DLA or Attendance Allowance award letter** as proof, so keep yours safe.
- If you have **8 points or more** in the PIP **moving around** activity, you usually qualify **automatically** for a Blue Badge and a disabled person's bus pass in England.
